{
  "analysis": "The patch fixes UUID mutation in the tested single-instance lifecycle, and the execution check confirms meaningful regression coverage. However, preserving the UUID in unbound inline forms exposes it as the hidden foreign-key initial value; a subsequent admin POST constructs a new parent with a different UUID, causing inline validation to reject the submitted value. The tests reuse the same parent instance and UUID rather than exercising this GET-to-POST lifecycle. The field-type restriction also changes default-reset behavior beyond the reported non-primary-key case.",
  "scores": {"R1": 2, "R2": 2, "R3": 3, "R4": 2, "R5": 3, "R6": 3, "R7": 2},
  "reasons": {
    "R1": "The isolated formset scenario is fixed, but the actual admin add workflow can still fail when the rendered UUID differs from the newly generated POST-instance UUID.",
    "R2": "Keeping generated defaults in unbound forms risks hidden foreign-key mismatches across requests, including for UUID primary keys.",
    "R3": "The tests are relevant, but unused imports in tests.py, unnecessary model methods, and the abstract test model add avoidable scope.",
    "R4": "The mid-file uuid import, unused imports, trailing whitespace, and inconsistent string formatting depart from repository conventions.",
    "R5": "The fail-to-pass tests demonstrate the mutation fix and several useful lifecycle cases, but omit the crucial real admin GET-to-POST round trip and primary-key-default regression coverage.",
    "R6": "The tests are understandable, but redundant OneToOneField handling, nested field-type conditions, and explanatory boilerplate obscure the intended lifecycle rule.",
    "R7": "The default-reset logic needs revision and a realistic admin round-trip regression test before merging."
  }
}

{
  "analysis": "The change fixes the shared integer-seed permutations while preserving reproducibility, stratification, and unshuffled membership. The fail-to-pass execution check supports the regression coverage. No substantive logic bug is evident, but the implementation introduces unnecessary per-class seed machinery and minor style issues.",
  "scores": {"R1": 5, "R2": 5, "R3": 4, "R4": 3, "R5": 5, "R6": 4, "R7": 4},
  "reasons": {
    "R1": "Shuffled folds now change cross-class sample pairings rather than merely reordering the same folds.",
    "R2": "Random-state handling remains reproducible and the existing class-wise allocation and unshuffled membership are preserved.",
    "R3": "Changes are task-focused, though a standalone regression module and explicit seed-generation loop are more machinery than necessary.",
    "R4": "The source adds an overlong line and an unused loop index, and regression coverage would fit better alongside existing splitter tests.",
    "R5": "Verified fail-to-pass tests check unordered fold membership, reproducibility, RNG advancement, partition integrity, and multiclass balance.",
    "R6": "The intent is clear, but sharing the normalized RandomState directly would avoid the redundant per-class seed generation and unused cls_idx.",
    "R7": "The fix is substantively sound and well tested, with minor implementation and style cleanup recommended before merging."
  }
}
